{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"educatory-toxic-eel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n`rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.git_run` folds a `TimeoutExpired` (300 s `_GIT_TIMEOUT`) into a private synthetic `CompletedProcess(rc=124, \"git timed out after 300s\")`. Its callers read that result as a semantic answer:\n\n- `rev_parse` returns `None` on any failure, so a timed-out `git rev-parse` makes `repo_snapshot.resolve_ref` raise `SnapshotRefError(\"cannot resolve ref … Name a valid branch, tag, or full SHA …\")` — a wrong-input verdict for a slow or wedged git call.\n- `has_remote` parses `git remote` stdout; a timeout yields empty stdout, so it answers \"no such remote\" and `resolve_ref` / `_ensure_blobs_present` skip the fetch path.\n- `is_present_full_sha` answers False (safe: it falls through to a fetch).\n\nFound by code reading while auditing private rc-124 folds for `unarmed-raw-siskin`. Not reproduced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git_run` uses `gitutil.run_git_bounded` instead of its private fold.\n- [ ] A timed-out `rev-parse` in `resolve_ref` is reported as a timeout naming the operation and bound, not as an unresolvable ref.\n- [ ] A timed-out `git remote` in `has_remote` is not read as \"remote absent\".\n- [ ] Regression tests drive each timeout and assert the report.","id":"d33f-b2ed-3d54-418c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["tracker","timeout","snapshot"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"git_fetch.git_run reads a timed-out rev-parse/remote as 'cannot resolve ref' / 'no remote'"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793692870682557001,"uuid":"70e2038b-a28b-4580-8d47-590a7b205108"}